// Vitest Snapshot v1, https://vitest.dev/guide/snapshot.html

exports[`buildPhotorealPrompt > matches the stored prompt for the full clay + id + references input 1`] = `
"Turn image 1 into a realistic photograph of this room, as if shot by a professional interior photographer.

Image 1 is a plain grey 3D "clay" render of the room. It fixes the camera and the layout:
- Keep the exact camera position, height, angle, lens and framing. Laid over image 1, the photo must line up with it.
- Keep every wall, door, window, radiator and piece of furniture exactly where it is, at the same size, proportions and orientation. Do not move, resize, rotate, add or remove anything.
- Change only surfaces and light: materials, colours, textures, reflections and shadows.

Image 2 is an ID map of the same view. Each piece of furniture is painted one flat colour so you can tell which item is which. The colours are labels, not paint: none of them may appear in the photo. Grey and white areas are the room itself.
- red: Auburn 3 Seater Sofa (product photo: image 3), about 14% of the frame — Curvy, low-slung 3-seater in chalk-white boucle.
- green: Jana Jute Rug (product photo: image 4), about 10% of the frame
- blue: 65in TV (no product photo), about 2% of the frame — Black flat-screen TV.
- orange and purple: 2 × Anya Dining Chair (product photo: image 5), about 1% of the frame — Chestnut-stained solid ash chair.

Images 3–5 are product photos of the actual pieces. Make each item look like its product: the same materials, colours, textures and details (legs, arms, edges, handles, weave). Keep its position, size and angle from image 1, and ignore the photo's own background, camera angle and lighting.

Room: Living room, about 2.98 m × 7.69 m (roughly rectangular, with a step in the outline), ceiling 2.45 m.
Finishes: walls soft warm white, matt; floor light natural oak boards, matt finish; ceiling white; skirting boards warm white, satin.
Styling: Calm, warm, Scandinavian-leaning interior: natural oak and walnut, boucle and linen, cream, sand and terracotta accents, soft daylight.
Camera: Eye-level view (1.6 m) from just inside the kitchen door (D1), looking towards the front window (WIN1). Daylight comes from the front window (WIN1), straight ahead.

Light: soft natural daylight through the window, gentle soft-edged shadows, a warm true-to-life white balance. Ceiling lights off.
Photo: eye-level interior photograph with a natural perspective and straight verticals, realistic materials, sharp focus, no people. No text, labels, watermarks or borders. Do not add furniture, rugs, plants, artwork, cushions, throws or decor that is not in image 1."
`;

